Template literals -> 

Template literals = backticks + ${} for injecting anything into a string.

what problem it solved
1. Normally we use '' or " " to write simple string, but when we need to add or inject any variable value or put any particular string in 
single or double quote, its hard to do in simple way.
EX: console.log('I love 'javascrip' coding') or console.log("i love 'javasript' codeing") its dificult to write.

2. Variable injection norally console.log('var' + variable_name) 

3. Multiline always we need to use \n 

4. No expression support that tends to write the code more messy 

Template literal solve this proble easily with ${} and 
we can put variable, 
it automatically pick up multiline however we write it prints the same on console 
support expression and more readable

console.log(`i love 'javasript' `)

let a = 100
console.log(`value of a is ${a}`)

let text = 'test'
console.log(`//span[text()='${text}']`)
